  "summary": "Enhancement – Emarsys Web Extend Integration (Cart Abandonment, Browse Abandonment & Revenue Tracking)",
  "description": "## Epic\n\nSFCC-24 – Enhancements\n\n## Background\n\nZimmermann currently uses Emarsys Web Extend on Magento to power three CRM flows: **cart abandonment**, **browse abandonment**, and **revenue contribution reporting**. These are direct browser-side integrations (3rd party JavaScript injection) and are separate from the client data CRM integration, which runs via Omneo → Mulesoft → Emarsys.\n\nBoth integrations must be replicated in SFCC — this story covers the **Web Extend** (JavaScript/browsing data) integration only. The Omneo/Mulesoft client data sync is covered separately.\n\nSAP Emarsys Web Extend documentation shared by Tessa Turnbull (Global CRM Director):\n\n- [https://help.sap.com/docs/SAP*EMARSYS/5d44574160f44536b0130abf58cb87cc/fdf50dbc74c1101495318ae4e0236a67.html?locale=en-US](https://help.sap.com/docs/SAP*EMARSYS/5d44574160f44536b0130abf58cb87cc/fdf50dbc74c1101495318ae4e0236a67.html?locale=en-US) \n- [https://help.sap.com/docs/SAP*EMARSYS/5d44574160f44536b0130abf58cb87cc/0e098e6a840d4832a0775b5acb0d24af.html?locale=en-US](https://help.sap.com/docs/SAP*EMARSYS/5d44574160f44536b0130abf58cb87cc/0e098e6a840d4832a0775b5acb0d24af.html?locale=en-US) \n\n----\n\n## Known Use Cases (in scope for analysis)\n\n1. **Cart Abandonment** – Emarsys sends a reminder email when a customer adds items to bag but does not complete checkout.\n1. **Browse Abandonment** – Emarsys sends a reminder email featuring a product the customer viewed but did not add to bag.\n1. **Revenue Contribution Reporting** – Web Extend captures revenue data for CRM reporting purposes.\n\n----\n\n## Outstanding Questions (to be resolved before story can be refined)\n\nThe following questions were raised by Jasmijn Tsang (6 July 2026) and have **not yet been answered** by Zimmermann:\n\n1. **Cart Abandonment – customer scope**: Is this triggered for logged-in customers only, or does it also apply to guest customers who have entered their email address at checkout entry?\n1. **Browse Abandonment – customer scope**: Is this working for logged-in customers only, or does it also apply to customers identified via a cookie from a previous session?\n1. **Additional CRM flows**: Are there any other CRM flows powered by Web Extend beyond the three identified above?\n\n----\n\n## Technical Considerations\n\n  - Web Extend is a **3rd party JavaScript injection* — scripts will need to be loaded on relevant SFCC pages.\n  - **TNL responsibility*: Confirm whether TNL (Zimmermann's team) will be configuring the rules, loading logic, and maintaining the Data Dictionary for click events and abandon events. Accenture to confirm scope boundary.\n  - **Data Dictionary*: Click Event and Abandon Event capture will need to be defined.",
