{"result":"{
  "id": "19449",
  "key": "SFCC-878",
  "summary": "Avalara Integration — Checkout Tax Calculation",
  "description": "**As a** Site Admin,\n**I want** Avalara integrated with SFCC\n**so that** the correct tax amount is calculated per product and jurisdiction at checkout across AU and US Domestic storefronts.\n\nAvalara (AvaTax) must be connected to SFCC via the SFCC Avalara cartridge to calculate GST, and state-level taxes at checkout for AU and US Domestic. At checkout, SFCC sends each line item with its `taxClassID` to Avalara; Avalara returns the correct tax amount per product based on the tax class, the Shopper's shipping address, and the applicable jurisdiction rules.\n\n**Not in scope:** \n\n- UK and EU Domestic uses SFCC native tax tables for VAT calculation, not Avalara and is covered in [SFCC-43](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-43).\n- Global-e handles its own tax for international markets (US International, EU International, HK, ME). \n\nFor AU cross-border orders to New Zealand and New Caledonia, Avalara's Landing Cost feature is active to return the duties cost. It returns two tax_types per line item: Output (GST equivalent) and LandedCost (duty). These are the only two AU destinations where Avalara Landing Cost fires, based on the confirmed `ddpCountries` configuration from the production AU storefront. Avalara uses the HS code and destination country to calculate applicable duties.\n\nHS codes are sourced from AP21 and synced to SFCC product attributes via MuleSoft.",
  "status": {
    "name": "In Refinement",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "# Given Avalara credentials and connection are configured in SFCC using the SFCC Avalara cartridge, when a checkout transaction is initiated on AU or US Domestic, then SFCC sends the transaction payload to Avalara including each line item with its taxClassID.\n# Given SFCC sends a transaction for the AU storefront and the Shopper's shipping address is within Australia, when Avalara calculates tax, then it returns a 10% GST amount per standard-rated line item and the total GST is applied to the order.\n# Given SFCC sends a transaction for the AU storefront and the Shopper's shipping address is in New Zealand or New Caledonia, when Avalara calculates the transaction using the Landing Cost feature, then it returns an tax amount and a duty amount per line item, and both are applied to the order.\n# Given SFCC sends a transaction for the US Domestic storefront, when Avalara calculates tax, then it applies the correct state-level sales tax per product tax class and the Shopper's shipping address. (Tax line item display is covered in SFCC-462.)\n# Given SFCC sends a transaction for the US Domestic storefront and the Shopper's shipping address is in Puerto Rico, when Avalara calculates the transaction using the Landing Cost feature, then it returns an tax amount and a duty amount per line item, and both are applied to the order.\n# Given the Avalara API is unavailable or returns an error at checkout, when SFCC attempts the call, then the failure is handled per the agreed fallback approach and checkout does not proceed with a missing or incorrect tax amount silently.\n\n[PENDING — UK and EU Domestic scope not yet confirmed:\n\n# Given SFCC sends a transaction for the UK storefront [if UK is confirmed in Avalara scope], when Avalara calculates tax, then it applies 20% VAT to standard-rated products and 0% VAT to products assigned the zero-rate tax class.\n# Given SFCC sends a transaction for the EU Domestic storefront [if EU Domestic is confirmed in Avalara scope], when Avalara calculates tax, then it applies the correct per-country VAT rate based on the destination country and the product's taxClassID."
  }
}"}

